42
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:47,320
Oh.

43
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,720
Rudeus.

44
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,800
Do you mind if I join you?

45
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:04,160
Not at all. Here, I even saved the seat for you.

46
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,780
Please sit. It's wonderful to see you again.

47
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,240
Thank you very much.

48
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:12,180
I feel like this guy really gets me.

49
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:15,220
How's your research going?

50
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,500
It's a little hard to tell.

51
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:20,920
Is that a book on teleportation?

52
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,160
Indeed.

53
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,340
I had been looking into the disaster myself.

54
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:27,400
Someone I know went missing, too.

55
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:31,720
I'm sorry. That's awful. I don't know what else to say.

56
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:35,840
It's all right. As a matter of fact, I've recently confirmed that he's alive.

57
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,160
Oh, really? That's great.

58
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:43,940
Yes. I never got the chance to search for him personally, so it was quite a relief.

59
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:55,040
That being said, I, uh, if you don't mind. And this is just a suggestion.

60
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:56,840
What is it?

61
00:04:56,840 --> 00:05:02,560
I would like you to let me help with your research into the displacement incident.

62
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:09,320
I'm often busy, though. So I could only pop in occasionally. But if that doesn't bother you...

63
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:14,220
That's fine, of course. I'd be delighted. It's a pleasure to have you on board.

64
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:22,840
No. Pleasure's mine.

65
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:27,900
Well, let's get started.

66
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:33,480
I thought this book could help us identify trends and where people ended up after their teleportation.

67
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:40,000
My heart fluttered. Am I seriously feeling this way about a guy?

68
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:52,960
I think Master Fitz and I have gotten closer. But there's still a lot I don't know about him.

69
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:58,540
I've been meaning to ask, do you wear those sunglasses all the time?

70
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:02,400
Sunglasses... Oh, right. You mean these.

71
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:07,840
Yes, but I can't tell you why, sadly. Apologies.

72
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:12,540
It's okay. I have another one, though. What floor of the dorms do you live on?

73
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:19,580
Oh, well, that's a little odd, too. I actually sleep in the girls' dorm, since I guard Princess Ariel.

74
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:22,900
And that doesn't, like, cause problems or anything?

75
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:29,740
No, it's fine. I have permission. And besides, I would never cause problems for Her Highness.

76
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:38,000
Dorms are segregated by gender, but servants and slaves of the opposite sex are allowed in, with permission.

77
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:41,060
As a student, Fitz doesn't fall into either category.

78
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:44,960
But it's not surprising that the school would make an exception for Princess Ariel's guard.

79
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:49,160
So, I've noticed that you talk to me pretty normally.

80
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,500
Oh? What do you mean?

81
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:54,020
You seem to be known as a man of few words.

82
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:58,020
Uh, yes. In truth, I'm awfully shy.

83
00:06:58,020 --> 00:07:04,540
I feel like he starts way too many conversations with me for that to be the case.

84
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:12,080
Oh, I also meant to ask, have you been casting without incantations since you were a child?

85
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:15,900
You're full of questions today, aren't you?

86
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:23,760
Yes. A long time ago, my master rescued me with voiceless magic, which is why I asked to start learning from him.

87
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:27,500
He's an amazing person, and I still look up to him to this day.

88
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:32,280
I had a master like that. I'd love it if I got to meet yours one day.

89
00:07:33,980 --> 00:07:36,800
Yes, well, it would be hard to introduce you.

90
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:39,240
Yeah? Why do you say that?

91
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:55,020
His smile definitely makes my heart skip a beat or two.

92
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:58,700
I was sure I didn't swing that way.

93
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:04,240
Well, I have business with Princess Ariel.

94
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:07,420
Understood. I can't wait to work with you again.

95
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:12,400
Silent Fitz, man of mystery.

96
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:17,200
I don't know why he's so willing to help me, but I'm not fussed about unraveling that right now.

97
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:23,100
Following the man-god's advice brought us together, so maybe sticking with him will eventually lead me to my cure.

98
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:24,940
No reason to worry.

99
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:28,720
Master!

100
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:32,220
Please, teach me how to sculpt figurines!

101
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,280
Then there's this guy.

102
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,340
A figurine pervert who would be banned from your local comic shop.

103
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:45,780
Just look at you.

104
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:47,920
You put the natural world to shame.

105
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:49,040
I am prepared to get your own...

106
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,380
This man loves figures.

107
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:52,600
Loves them.

108
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:56,060
But hey, I can see where he's coming from.

109
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:59,480
I might have enjoyed a figure or two in my past life.

110
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,880
You gave me your word, did you not, Master?

111
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:06,840
Why must you refuse yet again to begin my instruction?

112
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:10,540
I didn't promise him, and I have been brushing up.

113
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:13,000
I just haven't wanted to make the time.

114
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:15,740
This isn't what I came here to do.

115
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:22,540
Xanobah, understand my tutelage will be strict.

116
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:25,580
Yes, Master. I'm ready.

117
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:28,300
Very well. You've proven your resolve.

118
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,920
I shall now impart the secrets of my art.

119
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:31,920
Thank you, sir!

120
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:36,620
And thus, our great figurine enterprise began.

121
00:09:36,620 --> 00:10:05,080
Sorry.

122
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:07,180
So, blame yourself.

123
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:09,080
If only I were more skilled.

124
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:11,600
Well, hey. There's another way.

125
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:13,680
Yes! Teach me this other way, Master!

126
00:10:14,380 --> 00:10:14,820
Okay.

127
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:18,180
For this, we'll try to use as little magic as possible.

128
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:23,660
Oh, what are we going to do with that?

129
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:25,000
We'll carve it up.

130
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:28,300
Chiseling, carving...

131
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:30,660
It's not any easier than using magic,

132
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:32,960
but it's primitive, tried and true.

133
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:35,860
People with no mana at all have been doing it forever.

134
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:37,340
Spectacular!

135
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:38,220
Master!

136
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:40,640
I believe that even I can learn this art!

137
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:47,020
Xanobah just isn't very good with his hands.

138
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,900
His supernatural strength makes delicate,

139
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:52,680
detail-oriented work something of a challenge.

140
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:58,060
It's too hard!

141
00:10:58,800 --> 00:10:59,880
I can't do it!

142
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:02,960
I'll never be able to scum like you do, Master!

143
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:06,060
So, yeah.

144
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:08,200
That's what I was up to all of yesterday.

145
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:11,360
But you can already make figurines with magic?

146
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:12,320
Yeah.

147
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:14,700
See?

148
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:17,660
Are you kidding me?

149
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:18,520
That's amazing!

150
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,140
Nope, I can't do it.

151
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:29,120
That's not something your average caster can imitate.

152
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:30,760
I suppose it isn't.

153
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,480
And it's difficult to teach.

154
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,780
We also tried carving blocks of clay,

155
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:35,560
but you can imagine...

156
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:38,120
Yeah, he'd be too clumsy for that.

157
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:39,000
Right.

158
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,680
I don't know if it'll help,

159
00:11:41,900 --> 00:11:44,120
but I heard something around the Osoran capital

160
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:47,000
that sounded like it might be a similar type of case.

161
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:49,420
A similar case to Xanobah, you mean?

162
00:11:49,820 --> 00:11:50,200
Yes.

163
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:52,320
They wanted some personally crafted item,

164
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:54,740
but they lacked the talent and skill to do it themselves.

165
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:55,480
Okay.

166
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,340
How'd that person get around it?

167
00:11:58,020 --> 00:11:58,820
Well, um,

168
00:11:59,000 --> 00:11:59,820
if I recall,

169
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,940
they just got a slave to do it.

170
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:02,740
Oh.

171
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:04,980
Never would've crossed my mind.

172
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:07,440
I'll see how Xanobah feels about that.

173
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:10,240
Then maybe go to the market during our break next month.

174
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:11,080
Great.

175
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:12,600
Whatever you decide,

176
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:13,700
I hope it works out.

177
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:20,440
Is something wrong?

178
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,160
No, I just...

179
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,980
I have some time off, too.

180
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,240
Next break.

181
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:27,760
Oh, good.

182
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:28,560
You earned it.

183
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:30,160
Mm-hmm.

184
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:32,160
Uh...

185
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:34,160
Uh...

186
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:36,660
Well, in that case,

187
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:38,260
would you care to join us?

188
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:39,660
That okay?

189
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,380
I wouldn't be intruding?

190
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:43,200
No, of course you wouldn't.

191
00:12:43,460 --> 00:12:45,220
And I'll be happy to treat you to a meal

192
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:47,000
in exchange for all your advice.

193
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:47,960
All right.

194
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,040
I think I'll take you up on that.

195
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:56,800
I'm Fitz.

196
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:57,920
It's a...

197
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:58,960
Pleasure.

198
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:03,400
I am the Third Prince of the Chiron Kingdom.

199
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:04,600
My name is...

200
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:04,980
Xanobah!

201
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:06,940
Xanobah!

202
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:10,380
Master Fitz is the one who proposed this solution for your benefit.

203
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:12,320
Show him proper respect.

204
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:13,820
Understood, sir.

205
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:14,600
I'm sorry.

206
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,900
It is a pleasure to make your acquaintance.

207
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:17,980
Xanobah Chiron,

208
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:19,840
Third Prince of the Chiron Kingdom,

209
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:20,860
at your service.

210
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:22,760
Do forgive my indiscretion.

211
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:23,960
That's quite all right.

212
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:25,480
Really, please.

213
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,560
I take no offense, Your Highness.

214
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:28,780
Don't mind me.

215
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,180
I guess we ought to start moving then, huh?

216
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:33,140
Are you ready?

217
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:55,220
I see many fine displays.

218
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,000
Master, where shall we begin?

219
00:13:58,620 --> 00:13:59,380
No idea.

220
00:13:59,660 --> 00:14:00,920
I've never done this before.

221
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:03,020
Maybe just start by looking around.

222
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:12,940
Oh, wow.

223
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:15,700
So many of them are actually naked.

224
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:17,440
And so big.

225
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,100
I didn't know they got like that.

226
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,220
Spoken like a true virgin.

227
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:24,260
Yes.

228
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:26,140
Yes, I was one of you once.

229
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:28,180
And now...

230
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:30,440
Now I've got other things to worry about.

231
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:34,060
Are you used to seeing people like this, Rudeus?

232
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:38,140
Oh, I'm sure you'll get more comfortable with it once you gain some experience.

233
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:40,660
Sure, if you say so.

234
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:43,920
But wait, does that mean you have experience, then?

235
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:47,380
Master, these warriors are of no use.

236
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:52,800
We need to be looking for someone who's both magically gifted and naturally adept with their hands.

237
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:55,420
Okay, so who's known for their dexterity?

238
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,640
Maybe dwarves, I guess?

239
00:14:58,020 --> 00:15:04,680
And, well, if you intend to tutor them in magic, I think you should pick a child who doesn't know any yet.

240
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:05,520
At all?

241
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:07,900
Not if you can help it, no.

242
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:10,320
It can make voiceless magic easier.

243
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:12,180
Oh, can it really?

244
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:18,360
And if you start learning to cast by the time you're about five years old, it will do wonders for your mana capacity.

245
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:20,140
What makes you say that?

246
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:23,460
Most people seem to believe that mana capacity is set at birth.

247
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:29,220
That's what the textbooks say, but anecdotally, my master's case and mine prove them wrong.

248
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:30,580
It can expand.

249
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:32,260
I knew it.

250
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,520
I always suspected.

251
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:38,720
But if I started casting around two or three, that would explain my mana pool for sure.

252
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:42,860
Well, if we know who we're looking for, we should try to find a merchant.

253
00:15:44,380 --> 00:15:44,820
Hmm.

254
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:48,740
Yeah, we don't see dwarves of any age around here very often.

255
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:51,020
That might be a little hard to find for you.

256
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:53,580
If it helps, they don't have to be a dwarf.

257
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:55,980
They just need to be naturally dexterous.

258
00:15:56,460 --> 00:16:00,840
But we're also teaching magic, so it's more important to find someone young enough to pick it up.

259
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:01,480
Ah.

